<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21690" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">immĕmŏrābĭlis</span></b> 
			(<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inm-</span></b> ),
		e, adj.
		in-memorabilis (ante-class.). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Pass.</i>, <i>unmentionable</i>, <i>indescribable</i> = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀδιήγητος</span>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">spurcidioi versus immemorabiles,</span>”
				i. e. <i>unworthy to be mentioned</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Capt. prol. 56</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">spatium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr.
					6, 488</span></i>
			.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Act.</i>, <i>that will not tell any
				thing</i>, <i>speechless</i>, <i>silent</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">anus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut.
					Cist. 2, 2, 3</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
